PyKotor _LightHeader Binary Read/Write Order Fix
==================================================
File:  PyKotor/Libraries/PyKotor/src/pykotor/resource/formats/mdl/io_mdl.py
Class: _LightHeader  (lines ~2284-2391)

ROOT CAUSE
----------
The _LightHeader.read() method read fields in the wrong order:
  OLD (wrong):  unknown_arr (3 uint32 = 12 bytes) → flare arrays → flare_radius (float) → scalars
  NEW (correct): flare_radius (float = 4 bytes) → unknown_arr (3 uint32) → flare arrays → scalars

This caused a 4-byte misalignment for all subsequent fields.  When a light
node had non-zero flare array counts the misread counts were garbage values
(e.g. 15511) pointing far outside the file, causing:

    struct.error: unpack requires a buffer of 4 bytes

during _load_node(), which swallowed the exception and returned None from
load_model_from_bytes().  All 45 affected models (33 K1 + 12 K2) contained
at least one LIGHT node with an actual flare radius set; light nodes with
flare_radius=0 happened to be self-consistent under the wrong ordering and
passed silently.

EVIDENCE
--------
Binary data at the _LightHeader start for m33ab_02 light node at +0x3bdb:

  File offset 0x3c37 (= node_abs + 80):
  hex: 001b3749 00000000 00000000 00000000 003c9700 01000000 ...
       ^^^^^^^^ ^^^^                       ^^^^^^^^
       = 750000.0f (flare_radius)          = 0x3c97 (flare_sizes array offset)
         at +0x00                            at +0x10

  Under the OLD wrong reading:
    +0x00..0x0B = offset_to_unknown0/counts → reads 0x00493700 = 4,800,256 offset
    +0x0C..0x17 = offset_to_flare_sizes/counts → reads 0x00003c97 = 15511 (!!!)

  Under the CORRECT reading (flare_radius first):
    +0x00 = flare_radius = 750000.0   ✓
    +0x04..0x0F = unknown0 (all zeros) ✓
    +0x10 = offset_to_flare_sizes = 0x3c97 (valid in-file offset) ✓

REFERENCE
---------
Confirmed against kotorblender/io_scene_kotor/format/mdl/reader.py lines 247-259:

    if type_flags & NODE_LIGHT:
        flare_radius = self.mdl.read_float()          # ← float FIRST
        unknown_arr = self.get_array_def()             # ← then unknown array
        flare_size_arr = self.get_array_def()
        flare_position_arr = self.get_array_def()
        flare_color_shift_arr = self.get_array_def()
        flare_tex_name_arr = self.get_array_def()
        light_priority = self.mdl.read_int32()
        ambient_only = self.mdl.read_uint32()
        ...

Also confirmed against the wiki MDL-MDX-File-Format.md §Light header:
  Offset 0x00 : Unknown/Padding (16 bytes, first 4 bytes = flare_radius float)
  Offset 0x10 : Flare Sizes offset (uint32)
  ...
  Offset 0x40 : Light Priority  (NOT flare_radius here as code assumed)
  Total size  : 92 bytes

IMPACT
------
Before fix : 45 hard errors (33 K1 + 12 K2), all "load_model_from_bytes returned None"
After fix  : 0 errors — 3,304/3,304 module models pass (100%)

Affected game areas:
  K1: Manaan (m12x), Leviathan (m14x), Unknown World (m17x), Star Forge (m18x),
      Dantooine (m33x), cutscene SET files (m26x_set), various special modules
  K2: Dxun (421dxn), Onderon (50x/51xond), Dantooine (605dan), Droid planet (80xdro)

FIX APPLIED TO
--------------
PyKotor/Libraries/PyKotor/src/pykotor/resource/formats/mdl/io_mdl.py

Three changes:
1. _LightHeader.__init__(): moved self.flare_radius declaration to the top (before unknown0)
2. _LightHeader.read():  read flare_radius first (read_single()), then unknown0 array,
   then the 4 flare-data array triplets, then the 7 scalar fields — removed old
   read_single() at the end
3. _LightHeader.write(): write flare_radius first (write_single()), matching read order
